WEBVTT

00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:16.000
♪ You know Dasher and Dancer
and Prancer and Vixen ♪

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:28.000
♪ Comet and Cupid
and Donner and Blitzen ♪

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:40.000
♪ But do you recall
the most famous reindeer of all? ♪

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:52.000
♪ Rudolph the Red-Nosed Reindeer
had a very shiny nose ♪

00:00:52.000 --> 00:01:03.000
♪ And if you ever saw it,
you would even say it glows ♪

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:18.000
It was the day before Christmas,
and all through the hills

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:32.000
the reindeer were playing,
enjoying the spills

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:46.000
of skating and coasting
and climbing the willows,

00:01:46.000 --> 00:02:00.000
and hopscotch and leapfrog,
protected by pillows.

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:12.000
"Look, fellas! Look at his nose!
The sight! It's red!"

00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:26.000
Twice as big and twice as bright!
While most reindeers' noses

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:40.000
are brownish and tiny,
Rudolph's was red,

00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:54.000
very large and quite shiny.

00:02:54.000 --> 00:03:06.000
"Go on home, red nose!
Your mama's calling you!"

00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:20.000
"Come, come, Rudolph!
Tonight you hang up your stocking."

00:03:20.000 --> 00:03:34.000
While way, way up north,
on this dark, foggy night,

00:03:34.000 --> 00:03:48.000
awaiting the time
for his Christmas Eve flight,

00:03:48.000 --> 00:04:00.000
good old Santa knew
the fog would be hard to get through.

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:14.000
"Quick, quick! Get hitched in a hurry!
Dasher! Dancer! Prancer! Vixen!

00:04:14.000 --> 00:04:26.000
Comet! Cupid! Donner! Blitzen!"

00:04:26.000 --> 00:04:38.000
"To keep our direction,
you'll have to fly low!"

00:04:38.000 --> 00:04:50.000
"Come down here, quick!"
"Pretty close!"

00:04:50.000 --> 00:05:04.000
The air was still foggy,
the night dark and drear,

00:05:04.000 --> 00:05:16.000
when Santa arrived
at the home of the deer.

00:05:16.000 --> 00:05:28.000
But all this took time
and filled Santa with gloom,

00:05:28.000 --> 00:05:40.000
while slowly he groped
toward the next reindeer's room.

00:05:40.000 --> 00:05:52.000
The lamp wasn't burning.
The glow came instead

00:05:52.000 --> 00:06:04.000
from Rudolph's red nose
at the head of the bed!

00:06:04.000 --> 00:06:14.000
And then came the greatest idea
in all history!

00:06:14.000 --> 00:06:26.000
So Rudolph was told of the dark
and the delay,

00:06:26.000 --> 00:06:36.000
the fog and the blackness
and losing the way:

00:06:36.000 --> 00:06:46.000
"I need you tonight
to lead all my deer

00:06:46.000 --> 00:06:56.000
on the rest of our flight!"

00:06:56.000 --> 00:07:08.000
"Dear Mommy and Daddy,
I have gone to help Santa.

00:07:08.000 --> 00:07:18.000
Don't worry! — Rudolph (that's me)"

00:07:18.000 --> 00:07:28.000
"Hi, Rudolph! It's very dark here!"

00:07:28.000 --> 00:07:40.000
With Rudolph's red nose
as a wonderful light,

00:07:40.000 --> 00:07:50.000
old Santa flew quickly
the rest of the night.

00:07:50.000 --> 00:08:00.000
It all went so fast
that before it was day,

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:08.000
the very last present
was given away.

00:08:08.000 --> 00:08:14.000
"Yay! They've found Rudolph's message —
it's all over town!

00:08:14.000 --> 00:08:20.000
Now they'd do anything
only to please him!

00:08:20.000 --> 00:08:26.000
Rudolph, my boy,
they'll envy you now, far and near —

00:08:26.000 --> 00:08:32.000
no greater honor
can come to a deer

00:08:32.000 --> 00:08:38.000
than riding with Santa
and guiding his sleigh!"

00:08:38.000 --> 00:08:43.000
♪ Merry Christmas to all —
you'll go down in history! ♪
